### Daymark REST Client checks
### Set baseUrl to the URL printed by `npm run dev` (3000 or 3001).
### Use a unique testEmail for sign-up; change it before another new-account run.
### This file creates a persistent test account in your Neon database.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@testEmail = replace-with-unique-test-address@example.invalid
@testPassword = Replace-With-A-Temporary-Password-9482!

### OpenAPI schema used by /api-docs Swagger UI
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/open-api/generate-schema
Accept: application/json

### Signed-out session (200 with null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session
Accept: application/json

### Sign up (expects a new, unused testEmail; saves a user in the database)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "REST API Check",
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### Sign in using the same account (REST Client keeps the session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### Authenticated session (run after sign-up or sign-in)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session
Accept: application/json

### Sign out (clears the session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-out
Origin: {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Confirm signed-out session (200 with null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session
Accept: application/json

### Protected page (signed-out; should return a redirect to /sign-in)
# @no-redirect
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard

